      "commentary": "19:13\n\nNASB, TEV, JPSOA\n\"the household idol\"\n\nNKJV\n\"an image\"\n\nNRSV, Peshitta\n\"an idol\"\n\nNJB\n\"a domestic image\"\n\nREB\n\"their household god\"\n\nLXX\n\"the cenotaph\"\n\nThis MASCULINE PLURAL NOUN (BDB 1076) is difficult to define. There are no\ncognate roots. Why would David, who loves YHWH, have an idol/image in his home? See Hard Sayings of the Bible, p. 214.\n\nSPECIAL TOPIC: Teraphim\n\n▣\n\nNASB, NET (KB)\n\"quilt\"\n\nNKJV\n\"cover\"\n\nNRSV\n\"net\"\n\nTEV, Peshitta, RSV\n\"pillow\"\n\nNJB\n\"tress\"\n\nREB\n\"rug\"\n\nJPSOA\n\"cloth\"\n\nLXX\n\"liver\"\n\nThis NOUN (BDB 460, KB 458) appears only here. BDB suggests \"something netted.\""
